Title: The Long Way Down
Author: Plotkraft Demo

INT. DINER - NIGHT

Rain hammers the windows. MAYA, 30s, nurses cold coffee. A duffel bag sits at her feet.

MAYA
(to no one)
Twelve hours. That's all I need.

INT. DINER - CONTINUOUS

NOAH slides into the booth across from her. He is soaked through.

NOAH
You said you'd wait at the station.

MAYA
The station has cameras.

EXT. PARKING LOT - NIGHT

They cross to a rusted sedan. Noah checks the road behind them.

NOAH
If Kessler finds the bag before we do, we don't get a second run at this.

INT. SEDAN - MOVING - NIGHT

Maya unzips the duffel. Inside: a hard drive, wrapped in a hotel towel.

MAYA
It was never about the money.

EXT. KESSLER'S WAREHOUSE - DAWN

The sedan idles across the street. Lights burn in a second-floor window.

NOAH
That's his office. Second floor.

INT. WAREHOUSE - STAIRWELL - CONTINUOUS

Maya climbs alone. Every step is a decision she can't take back.

INT. WAREHOUSE - OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

KESSLER waits, unsurprised, a second hard drive already on the desk.

KESSLER
You brought me a copy of my own file.

MAYA
I brought you the only one that still works.
